    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **266 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner `initials` field following the existing pattern used for `displayName` (cp06):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n   This produces e.g. `\"J.S.\"` \u2014 first letter of first and last name, upper-cased, dot-separated with a trailing dot.\n\nSince the mapper is used for both the create response and the get response, the new field is populated wherever an owner is serialized. The `Cp07Tests` acceptance test (`$.initials` == `\"J.S.\"`) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
